// runner.cla: the toolbox suite's enum, dispatch, and self-check
// (test-suite-review Task 11) -- the Mac-only sibling of
// testsuite/core/runner.cla, seeded with the audit's first three real
// Ch13 cases: TickCountAdvances (cases_events.cla), MenuKeyMatches
// (cases_events.cla), CanvasChecksum (cases_draw.cla), plus a fourth
// added by Task 13's own coverage-honesty audit: A5Live (cases_a5.cla).
// Every real case
// runs SYNCHRONOUSLY, in-process, exercising a REAL Toolbox trap or a
// REAL QuickDraw framebuffer read -- the paths no scripted golden
// reaches (a scripted `--events` build routes time through
// gVirtualTicks and menu keys through the script engine, never through
// the real UiTickCount/UiMenuKey trap dispatch -- see
// testdata/cg68k/tickprobe.cla's own header comment for the regression
// this suite's TickCountAdvances/MenuKeyMatches cases pin). Shape
// (enum/tbCaseName/tbAllCases/tbHas/dedupe+wantAll dispatch/SelfCheck
// last) mirrors testsuite/core/runner.cla's own CoreTest shape exactly,
// `tb`-prefixed (house style: the runtime extern-prefix convention,
// applied here so this suite's identifiers never collide with core's if
// the two suites are ever composed together, even though nothing does
// that today). GestaltNamed (cases_gestalt.cla) is Task 2's own addition
// (toolbox-integration): the generalized named-register trap clause's
// native gate. EventXRec (cases_event.cla) is Task 6's own addition
// (toolbox-integration Feature B): `extern record` native storage/decay
// against a real OSEventAvail trap. UiTestVerbSmoke/PostEventClick
// (cases_uitest.cla) are Task 3's own addition (ui-scenario-retirement):
// the `UiTest*` driver surface (uitest.cla) end to end, plus a REAL
// PostEvent-queued click against harness.cla's UiProbe window. Pattern
// (cases_pattern.cla) is Task 4's own addition (ui-scenario-retirement
// pilot migration): the retired testdata/ui/pattern.cla golden UI
// scenario, migrated to five UiTestChecksum region assertions against
// harness.cla's PatBoard window -- see cases_pattern.cla's own header
// comment for the full retirement mapping. Buttons/Winvar/Textwidgets
// (cases_buttons.cla/cases_winvar.cla/cases_textwidgets.cla) are Task 5's
// own addition (ui-scenario-retirement batch migration): the retired
// testdata/ui/buttons.cla, winvar.cla, and textwidgets.cla golden UI
// scenarios, migrated to ButtonsPanel/LogWin/TextWin cases against
// harness.cla's own windows of the same names -- see each case file's own
// header comment for its full retirement mapping. Menus/Editmenu
// (cases_menus.cla/cases_editmenu.cla) are Task 6's own addition
// (ui-scenario-retirement batch migration): the retired
// testdata/ui/menus.cla and editmenu.cla golden UI scenarios, migrated to
// MenuMain/MenuAux/Ops and EditMain/Edit cases against harness.cla's own
// windows/menus of the same names -- see each case file's own header
// comment for its full retirement mapping. Canvas/Zoomwin/Hscroll
// (cases_canvas.cla/cases_zoomwin.cla/cases_hscroll.cla) are Task 7's own
// addition (ui-scenario-retirement batch migration): the retired
// testdata/ui/canvas.cla, zoomwin.cla, and hscroll.cla golden UI
// scenarios, migrated to CanvasWin, ZoomWin, and HScrollWin/HFitWin cases
// against harness.cla's own windows of the same names -- see each case
// file's own header comment for its full retirement mapping.
// Popuptable (cases_popuptable.cla) is Task 8's own addition
// (ui-scenario-retirement batch migration): the retired
// testdata/ui/popuptable.cla golden UI scenario, migrated to the
// PopupTableWin window Task 8 also added to harness.cla -- see that case
// file's own header comment for its full retirement mapping. Task 8's own
// OTHER scenario, formedit, was NOT migrated at the time: the migration
// attempt uncovered a real native-68k (cg68k) codegen bug in a form's
// `accepted(rec: T)` event marshaling (a bound `bool` field silently
// reverts to `false` even when the live control reads `true` at every
// point up to and including inside the accepted handler itself) -- see
// task-8-report.md for the full investigation. See the FormEdit paragraph
// below for its eventual migration once that bug was fixed.
// Dialogs/Hdim (cases_dialogs.cla/cases_hdim.cla) are Task 9's own
// addition (ui-scenario-retirement batch migration): the retired
// testdata/ui/dialogs.cla and hdim.cla golden UI scenarios, migrated to
// the DialogsWin and DimWin windows Task 9 also added to harness.cla --
// see each case file's own header comment for its full retirement
// mapping. FormEdit (cases_formedit.cla) is test-consolidation Task 3's
// own addition: the previously-unmigrated testdata/ui/formedit.cla golden
// UI scenario, now that its blocking native-68k codegen bug (a form's
// trailing `bool` field silently reverting to `false` on `accepted(rec)`
// writeback) was fixed by small-scalar-width commit 8278ae7 -- see
// harness.cla's own FormEditWin comment and cases_formedit.cla's own
// header comment for the full migration mapping and bug history.
// BigText (cases_bigtext.cla) is test-consolidation Task 4's own
// addition: migrates the retired native-only `TestTexteditorBigfileOn68k`/
// `TestTexteditorBigfileUIScenario` boots (audit rows N17/R10) into a
// >32,000-byte textview SET + clamp + `lastError` + tail-content-exact
// case against harness.cla's existing TextWin window (no harness.cla
// change needed) -- see cases_bigtext.cla's own header comment for the
// full assertion mapping and what stays native-only (the example app's
// own alert-message/close-cascade guard logic). Catalog (cases_catalog.cla)
// is toolbox-cookbook Task 2's own addition: hardware-proves the shipped
// toolbox/{memory,events,osutils,scrap}.cla extern catalog by calling it
// against real ROM, in-process -- see cases_catalog.cla's own header
// comment. FInfoStamp (cases_finfo.cla) is native-gaps-cleanup Task 3's
// own addition: hardware-proves Tasks 1-2's file.writeText stamp rule
// (app.doctype/app.id compile-time defaults, exact 4CC pass-through) by
// reading the written files' real Finder type/creator back via
// PBGetFInfoSync -- see cases_finfo.cla's own header comment.
// ResourceBake/WriteResStamp (cases_resources.cla) are Task 7's own
// addition (mac-resident-clarusc phase): hardware-prove the new
// `file.readResource`/`file.writeRes` intrinsics -- a real
// Get1NamedResource lookup against a `--bake`d 'CLFS' resource (content
// + missing-name failure) and a real resource-fork write re-statted via
// the same PBGetFInfoSync pattern FInfoStamp uses -- see
// cases_resources.cla's own header comment. DateTimeRoundTrip
// (cases_datetime.cla) is datetime-instrumentation Task 7's own
// addition: hardware-proves the Date-Time Utilities catalog contracts
// (SecondsToDate/DateToSeconds, toolbox/osutils.cla) and the
// now()/dateTimeStr builtins against real ROM -- see
// cases_datetime.cla's own header comment. LivePaint (cases_textwidgets.cla)
// is the live-log phase's own Task 1 addition: hardware-proves that
// programmatic textview/label sets (rtUiWidgetSetText / rtUiWidgetSetStr's
// label branch, uiwidgets.cla) paint SYNCHRONOUSLY, before any update
// event can run -- see that case's own header comment for the full
// checksum-region derivation. SerialOpenWrite (cases_serial.cla) is
// serial-connection phase Task 2's own addition: hardware-proves the
// toolbox/devices.cla + toolbox/serial.cla Device Manager/Serial Driver
// catalog by opening the real .AOut/.AIn drivers, configuring 9600-8N1,
// exercising the load-bearing SerSetBuf call, writing 5 bytes, and
// reading a real SerGetBuf count -- see that case's own header comment.
// NarrowPopup (cases_narrowpopup.cla) is correctness-cleanup Task 2's own
// addition: hardware-proves the labeled-popup layout fix
// (uiwidgets.cla's new rtUiKindPopup-with-label arm +
// rtUiPopupBoxInto's defensive floor, uitable.cla) against a real
// `width: 60` labeled popup (harness.cla's NarrowPopupWin) -- see that
// case's own header comment. LeakCheck (cases_leak.cla) is
// 68k-call-result-release Task 4's own addition: hardware-proves that a
// user function's text result consumed directly (argument / operand /
// receiver / builtin-method-argument) is released by the emit68k
// call-result-release fix -- a real FreeMem-flat proof across thousands
// of direct-consumption iterations on the emulator, complementing
// internal/cg68k/callresult_release_test.go's listing-level pin.

enum ToolboxTest {
    All
    TickCountAdvances
    MenuKeyMatches
    CanvasChecksum
    A5Live
    GestaltNamed
    EventXRec
    UiTestVerbSmoke
    PostEventClick
    Pattern
    Buttons
    Winvar
    Textwidgets
    Menus
    Editmenu
    Canvas
    Zoomwin
    Hscroll
    Popuptable
    Dialogs
    Hdim
    FormEdit
    FieldCap
    BigText
    Catalog
    FInfoStamp
    ResourceBake
    WriteResStamp
    DateTimeRoundTrip
    LivePaint
    SerialOpenWrite
    NarrowPopup
    LeakCheck
    SelfCheck
}

// nTbCases is ToolboxTest's member count minus All: the 32 real cases
// plus SelfCheck itself. Same "SelfCheck's own branch does not increment
// casesRun for itself" convention as CoreTest's nCoreCases (runner.cla) --
// a forgotten branch leaves casesRun short and SelfCheck fails instead of
// the suite silently shrinking.
const nTbCases: int = 33

// tbCaseName maps a ToolboxTest member to its programmatic name, used as
// both the GUI's table row label and a TestResult's name.
func tbCaseName(t: ToolboxTest): string {
    switch t {
    case All {
        return "All"
    }
    case TickCountAdvances {
        return "TickCountAdvances"
    }
    case MenuKeyMatches {
        return "MenuKeyMatches"
    }
    case CanvasChecksum {
        return "CanvasChecksum"
    }
    case A5Live {
        return "A5Live"
    }
    case GestaltNamed {
        return "GestaltNamed"
    }
    case EventXRec {
        return "EventXRec"
    }
    case UiTestVerbSmoke {
        return "UiTestVerbSmoke"
    }
    case PostEventClick {
        return "PostEventClick"
    }
    case Pattern {
        return "Pattern"
    }
    case Buttons {
        return "Buttons"
    }
    case Winvar {
        return "Winvar"
    }
    case Textwidgets {
        return "Textwidgets"
    }
    case Menus {
        return "Menus"
    }
    case Editmenu {
        return "Editmenu"
    }
    case Canvas {
        return "Canvas"
    }
    case Zoomwin {
        return "Zoomwin"
    }
    case Hscroll {
        return "Hscroll"
    }
    case Popuptable {
        return "Popuptable"
    }
    case Dialogs {
        return "Dialogs"
    }
    case Hdim {
        return "Hdim"
    }
    case FormEdit {
        return "FormEdit"
    }
    case FieldCap {
        return "FieldCap"
    }
    case BigText {
        return "BigText"
    }
    case Catalog {
        return "Catalog"
    }
    case FInfoStamp {
        return "FInfoStamp"
    }
    case ResourceBake {
        return "ResourceBake"
    }
    case WriteResStamp {
        return "WriteResStamp"
    }
    case DateTimeRoundTrip {
        return "DateTimeRoundTrip"
    }
    case LivePaint {
        return "LivePaint"
    }
    case SerialOpenWrite {
        return "SerialOpenWrite"
    }
    case NarrowPopup {
        return "NarrowPopup"
    }
    case LeakCheck {
        return "LeakCheck"
    }
    case SelfCheck {
        return "SelfCheck"
    }
    }
    return "?"
}

// tbAllCases lists every real case (All excluded; SelfCheck included) --
// the GUI's table row order (gui.cla's App.startEmpty).
func tbAllCases(): list of ToolboxTest {
    var l: list of ToolboxTest
    l.add(TickCountAdvances)
    l.add(MenuKeyMatches)
    l.add(CanvasChecksum)
    l.add(A5Live)
    l.add(GestaltNamed)
    l.add(EventXRec)
    l.add(UiTestVerbSmoke)
    l.add(PostEventClick)
    l.add(Pattern)
    l.add(Buttons)
    l.add(Winvar)
    l.add(Textwidgets)
    l.add(Menus)
    l.add(Editmenu)
    l.add(Canvas)
    l.add(Zoomwin)
    l.add(Hscroll)
    l.add(Popuptable)
    l.add(Dialogs)
    l.add(Hdim)
    l.add(FormEdit)
    l.add(FieldCap)
    l.add(BigText)
    l.add(Catalog)
    l.add(FInfoStamp)
    l.add(ResourceBake)
    l.add(WriteResStamp)
    l.add(DateTimeRoundTrip)
    l.add(LivePaint)
    l.add(SerialOpenWrite)
    l.add(NarrowPopup)
    l.add(LeakCheck)
    l.add(SelfCheck)
    return l
}

// tbHas reports whether l contains want.
func tbHas(l: list of ToolboxTest, want: ToolboxTest): bool {
    var t: ToolboxTest
    for t in l {
        if t == want {
            return true
        }
    }
    return false
}

// runToolboxTests dedupes sel, then runs every selected case's branch --
// same dedupe/wantAll/branch shape as testsuite/core/runner.cla's
// runCoreTests. Each dispatch arm is its own statement, so the per-statement
// temp-slot budget holds regardless of case count -- 32 real cases here,
// and this dispatch never approaches the budget. (Unlike core's cli.cla
// arg-matching loop, which needs careful iteration to stay within budget;
// see coreMatchAndAdd's doc comment in testsuite/core/cli.cla. Moot here
// besides: this suite has no CLI front end).
func runToolboxTests(sel: list of ToolboxTest): list of TestResult {
    var deduped: list of ToolboxTest
    var t: ToolboxTest
    var results: list of TestResult
    var wantAll: bool
    var casesRun: int = 0
    var selfDetail: string

    for t in sel {
        if not tbHas(deduped, t) {
            deduped.add(t)
        }
    }
    wantAll = tbHas(deduped, All)

    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, TickCountAdvances) {
        results.add(caseTickCountAdvances())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, MenuKeyMatches) {
        results.add(caseMenuKeyMatches())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, CanvasChecksum) {
        results.add(caseCanvasChecksum())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, A5Live) {
        results.add(caseA5Live())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, GestaltNamed) {
        results.add(caseGestaltNamed())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, EventXRec) {
        results.add(caseEventXRec())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, UiTestVerbSmoke) {
        results.add(caseUiTestVerbSmoke())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, PostEventClick) {
        results.add(casePostEventClick())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Pattern) {
        results.add(casePattern())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Buttons) {
        results.add(caseButtons())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Winvar) {
        results.add(caseWinvar())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Textwidgets) {
        results.add(caseTextwidgets())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Menus) {
        results.add(caseMenus())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Editmenu) {
        results.add(caseEditmenu())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Canvas) {
        results.add(caseCanvas())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Zoomwin) {
        results.add(caseZoomwin())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Hscroll) {
        results.add(caseHscroll())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Popuptable) {
        results.add(casePopuptable())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Dialogs) {
        results.add(caseDialogs())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Hdim) {
        results.add(caseHdim())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, FormEdit) {
        results.add(caseFormEdit())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, FieldCap) {
        results.add(caseFieldCap())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, BigText) {
        results.add(caseBigText())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, Catalog) {
        results.add(caseCatalog())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, FInfoStamp) {
        results.add(caseFInfoStamp())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, ResourceBake) {
        results.add(caseResourceBake())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, WriteResStamp) {
        results.add(caseWriteResStamp())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, DateTimeRoundTrip) {
        results.add(caseDateTimeRoundTrip())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, LivePaint) {
        results.add(caseLivePaint())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, SerialOpenWrite) {
        results.add(caseSerialOpenWrite())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, NarrowPopup) {
        results.add(caseNarrowPopup())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, LeakCheck) {
        results.add(caseLeakCheck())
        casesRun = casesRun + 1
    }
    if wantAll or tbHas(deduped, SelfCheck) {
        if casesRun == nTbCases - 1 {
            results.add(tkPass(tbCaseName(SelfCheck)))
        } else {
            selfDetail = "casesRun " + tkIntToStr(casesRun) + " != " + tkIntToStr(nTbCases - 1)
            results.add(tkFail(tbCaseName(SelfCheck), selfDetail))
        }
    }

    return results
}
